values ('Total solar eclipse over Luxor: Luxor, 2027-08-02', 'A total solar eclipse crosses Upper Egypt on Monday 2 August 2027. Near Luxor, totality lasts up to about six minutes, the longest on land until 2114 (NASA gives a central duration of 6 minutes 23 seconds).', 'CALENDAR_EVENT', 'TRAVEL', 'EGYPT', 'QUALIFIED', 'NEW', 'SOURCE_BACKED', 'Claude (Private Calendar research, 4 Oct 2026)', 'VERIFIED', 'EGYPT', 'Luxor', null, 'Egypt', 'Luxor', '2027-08-02', '2027-08-02', 'https://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/SEgoogle/SEgoogle2001/SE2027Aug02Tgoogle.html', 'NASA Goddard Space Flight Center', '2026-10-04', 95, 100, 60, 100, 'total-solar-eclipse-luxor-2027', 'calendarEvent.total-solar-eclipse-luxor-2027', 'solar-eclipse-luxor|2027-08', 'Date and duration checked on 4 Oct 2026 against NASA''s eclipse page; also Forbes (16 Aug 2026) and the National Solar Observatory map. Egypt''s tourism ministry has a hosting committee (Ahram Online, reported). Lead time matters: Luxor hotels and Nile boats are expected to sell out early. August heat above 40°C. Awaiting CEO approval. Scores: initial NOYA judgement.')
